NAME
    bootid - this boot's identity, as the kernel established it

SYNOPSIS
    bootid

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the boot counter the kernel raised and persisted before leaving
    the firmware, which stores held a counter from before this boot (the
    UEFI non-volatile variable, the file \EFI\ORBS\BOOTID.TXT on the ESP),
    and how many bytes of boot entropy the firmware supplied.

    A counter counts only if a store held one before this boot. With none,
    "no boot counter this boot" is printed, and the node keys no cluster
    sessions.

    It also asks for the boot entropy itself, which the kernel gives to the
    network server alone, and reports the refusal.

EXIT STATUS
    0 with a counter, 1 without one, 2 if the kernel handed this program
    the boot entropy.

SEE ALSO
    edtest - the on-target check of the session-auth crypto
